# Binary assets, marked so no checkout ever rewrites their line endings.
#
# Git guesses text-or-binary by looking for NUL bytes near the start of a file,
# and a PDF whose first stream happens not to have one is guessed wrong. Adding
# docs/texel-emitters-design.pdf produced "LF will be replaced by CRLF the next
# time Git touches it" on a 570 KB binary -- harmless in this working tree,
# because the blob went in untouched, and a corrupted file on the next clone
# with core.autocrlf set the other way.
#
# The images have survived on luck rather than on a rule. This is the rule.
*.pdf   binary
*.png   binary
*.jpg   binary
*.jpeg  binary
*.ico   binary
*.ttf   binary
*.otf   binary
*.fbx   binary
*.glb   binary
*.dll   binary
*.exe   binary
*.wav   binary
*.ogg   binary

# Cooked and packed containers: the import cache's own formats.
*.rvtx  binary
*.rvmesh binary
*.rvpak binary
